      "note": "Reads v->via.str.ptr/size as if v were a string even though v->type was never checked; if the time_key value is actually a non-string msgpack type (int, map, array, etc.), this reinterprets unrelated union bytes as a pointer and length, causing an invalid/out-of-bounds memory access."
